            <ArticleTitle>[Intracranial hypotension and sixth cranial nerve palsy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The sixth cranial nerves may be involved in rare cases of post-puncture syndrome after lumbar anesthesia as well as in cases of spontaneous intracranial hypotension. We present 3 cases of spontaneous intracranial hypotension with unilateral or bilateral sixth nerve palsy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
